{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the carried exact-path succession repair at ea11839271af369baca9b6f79d7aefb48f48af56 (request/specific-path-succession-carried, one commit on reviewed c0df0efd, three on main c3169d83; exactly the eight cited paths; Rests-On repair request 979ffab3; request 15360 rests on the repair request and the eight ea118392 artifacts, none stale). Review against request 15360; not merged.\n\nBoth blockers from my ratified verdict f40d3898 are fixed and mutation-proved on a detached checkout. N1: a new leftLiveCarried class; successionPredecessors computes target-world membership independently (the merge-base probe runs per covered artifact, memoised by commit) and splits in-target changed-lineage artifacts into predecessors, in-target unchanged wider pointers into carried, and outside-world candidates into sibling or abandoned; the fixture whose board line last round read \"abandoned artifact #8, retirement owed by @reviewer\" now reads \"carried current artifact #8\", with receipt class carried, fold verified with empty reason, the docs pointer live, fresh, successionUnrecorded false and no omitted supersessions; succession.go:98-101 and :255-258 and merge.md:250 are now true. N2: dropping artifactRetiresForChanges from the in-target branch fails TestMergeClassifiesEveryCoveredLiveArtifact at succession_test.go:79 on both the main-ancestor and candidate arms. Seventeen mutations red in all, including four new fold-level guards (carried case removed, carried accepting a commitment, carried dropping the wider check, render carried as abandoned) and every earlier proof at its new lines, with the cross-author guard still proved end to end. Gates: gofmt, go build, go vet, git diff --check c0df0efd..ea118392 clean; go test ./... -count=1 all 34 packages ok including internal/docset. The two simplification items the request made mechanical are done (the dead widerPath tie-break removed; leaveLive returns a bool and assign calls it).\n\nTwo changes before approval.\n\n1. The fold's projection changed for a fixed log and ProfileVersion did not. internal/workroom/schema.go:16 still says workroom-fold@15, while validateMergeLeftLiveNow gains case \"carried\" (fold.go:1586) and its default reason changes to \"class must be carried, sibling, or abandoned\" (fold.go:1613). Folding one fixed log carrying a carried receipt under both binaries: the new fold projects Verified true with an empty reason and renders \"carried current artifact #11\"; the old fold projects Verified false with \"class must be sibling or abandoned\" and renders an UNVERIFIED line; both stamp @15. Statement.MergeLeftLive is a projected, cached, API-exposed field and the projection cache is keyed on application plus ProfileVersion (internal/app/host.go:34), so two binaries at the same profile now produce different projections of the same log and either can serve or accept the other's cache, which is exactly what the profile gate exists to prevent; architecture.md states the rule at :798-799 and :1204 and every prior fold change in that file carries the \"advances the profile\" sentence, absent from the new carried paragraph at :845-849. Nothing catches the omission because internal/app/app_test.go:2378, :2444 and :2519 hardcode @15 as the wanted profile. The divergence is in projected evidence, not in any decision or authority (an old binary reading a new receipt degrades to an unverified entry with no debt), so this is cache correctness and displayed truth, not split authority; it is still the repo's own invariant violated silently. Bump the profile, update the three literals, and add the profile sentence to architecture.md. Coordinate with the staleness write-boundary head on request/stale-basis-admission-current, which already advances to workroom-fold@16 and is approved and awaiting a merge decision: whichever of the two lands second takes @17, and the architecture history should record both.\n\n2. AGENTS.md and SKILL.md still teach the two-class world. AGENTS.md:75-80 says a pointer wider than a landed destination is sealed \"as either a sibling protected by its unsettled commitment or an abandoned candidate\" and that the abandoned candidate's author or a ratifier retires it; SKILL.md:234-238 says merge_left_live classifies every other covering candidate as a protected sibling or as abandoned, and SKILL.md:269 calls the abandoned classification the durable prompt for cleanup. The first is the very sentence I quoted last round as instructing an author to retire a healthy pointer, and AGENTS.md is what every agent reads, so the operator-facing half of N1 is unfixed. Repair request 15329 scoped the change to merge.md and architecture.md and forbade broadening, so the implementer complied; this needs an amendment to 15329 or a child rather than a fault finding, and both pages should describe carried and confine sibling and abandoned to outside-world candidates.\n\nRecorded, not blocking. A carried claim is verified on the merger's word: the fold checks only that it names no commitment and is not at or below a landed successor, and for a genuine wider pointer no published path covers it, so the second check never runs; an outside-world candidate sealed carried verifies and renders as current where abandoned would have rendered a cleanup prompt owed to its author, so a merger can quietly drop another actor's cleanup prompt (no authority moves and no debt forms either way); the fold holds no repository and cannot check target-world membership, which merge.md:276-279 should say as it already does for the refutable abandoned claim. architecture.md:850 is a 96-column line among 70-78-column neighbours. The removed branch still scans covering(path, true) for the exact match and then covering(path, false) for the rest, two passes over live, deferred by the request. A1 to A3 (a directory pointer over a modify-only merge is now truthfully carried but is never retired or refreshed and silently ages; one